{"id": "EUVD-2026-87322", "enisaUuid": "4f7c78ef-1693-3725-bc86-fa241eceffcc", "description": "phar_tar_number() parses the octal size field of a TAR header into a uint32_t with no overflow check. The field is 11 octal digits wide and holds values up to 0x1FFFFFFFF, so a size above 0xFFFFFFFF silently wraps. The parser then skips the wrong number of data blocks and interprets attacker-controlled file content as the next TAR header, which lets a crafted archive inject entries that PharData reports and extracts as if they were genuine.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T20:08:49", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-25T20:41:27", "baseScore": 4.3, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:N/I:L/A:N", "references": ["https://github.com/php/php-src/security/advisories/GHSA-j3wh-g957-2m85"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-6103"], "assigner": "php", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2e91e142-ac8e-3282-bea3-ebefebf7f49c", "product": {"name": "PHP", "vendor": {"name": "PHP Group"}}, "product_version": "8.2.* <8.2.34"}, {"id": "91966da2-adca-3855-9093-22a38a039ba0", "product": {"name": "PHP", "vendor": {"name": "PHP Group"}}, "product_version": "8.4.* <8.4.26"}, {"id": "c7c2c624-93f4-3b65-ab61-3c50e649c733", "product": {"name": "PHP", "vendor": {"name": "PHP Group"}}, "product_version": "8.5.* <8.5.11"}, {"id": "ec2993f2-de8f-3f77-ae7c-c4cdd577cc8e", "product": {"name": "PHP", "vendor": {"name": "PHP Group"}}, "product_version": "8.3.* <8.3.35"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "78e564aa-4c19-31f6-84bd-7b62a3d4555d", "vendor": {"name": "PHP Group"}}], "isExploited": false}